---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const entries = (await getCollection('scenarios')).sort((a, b) => (a.data.order ?? 99) - (b.data.order ?? 99));
---
<Base title="Real situations" lang="en" description="Twelve everyday moments where personal data changes hands in Sri Lanka, and what the law says about each.">
  <h1>Real situations</h1>
  <p>The Act is 57 sections long. Most people meet it in a handful of ordinary moments. Each page below shows which sections apply, from when, what to do now, and the things people commonly get wrong.</p>
  <div class="scenarios">{entries.map((s, i) => <a href={`/en/scenarios/${s.id}/`}><span class="n">{i + 1}</span><span>{s.data.title}</span></a>)}</div>
  <figure><a class="zoom" href="/img/data-lifecycle.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/img/data-lifecycle.svg" alt="Five stages: collect, use, keep, share, delete, with the duty at each stage" width="1000" height="300" /></a><figcaption>Whatever the situation, the same five steps apply from 1 January 2027.</figcaption></figure>
</Base>
